        "A Gersmehl diagram represents nutrient stores in biomass, litter and soil, linked by transfers. Litterfall transfers nutrients from living organisms into dead material; decomposition releases nutrients to soil and roots take them up. Rainfall deposition and weathering can add nutrients, while leaching and removal can export them. Temperate woodland often has a substantial soil store; relative stores and rates vary, so schematic circle sizes are not universal measured percentages."
